-- examples/checks/agg-wfs-declares.rofl — below agg_cell_wfs beside the game:
-- rules that conclude what the kernel reads as a declaration. A declaration
-- is no answer, so neither is fed: `semantics(well_founded)` fed would make
-- the world above well-founded and refuse its cells, and `sealed(provenance)`
-- would seal the provenance of a world that never asked. And a relation
-- that is both input and concluded: every row of it that holds is an answer,
-- the asserted one too (wd_p(a) and wd_p(b) are fed), while wd_q, input that
-- no rule concludes, is not.
edb(wd_mode).
wd_mode(well_founded). wd_mode(provenance).
semantics(S) :- wd_mode(S), S = well_founded.
sealed(S)    :- wd_mode(S), S = provenance.
edb(wd_q).
wd_q(b).
wd_p(a).
wd_p(X) :- wd_q(X).
